# WardenClyffe Boundary-Guard Rule (forced)

During development, **before creating any new folder, module, package, service,
or domain boundary**, run the duplicate check first so a new boundary is not a
duplicate of an existing one.

Follow `docs/ai/WARDENCLYFFE_BOUNDARY_GUARD_SKILL.md`.

```bash
python scripts/foundation/boundary-guard-tree.py --snapshot
python scripts/foundation/boundary-guard-tree.py --diff
python scripts/foundation/boundary-guard-tree.py --check "<proposed/path>"
```

Exit code `2` means a likely duplicate — reuse the existing boundary. Creating a
genuinely new domain requires operator approval.
